    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing our highest offensive floor at an 87.42. He faces a highly favorable matchup against Rodr\u00edguez, whose 5.91 xERA suggests he will struggle to contain **Yordan Alvarez**'s elite .458 xwOBA; combined with a strong park factor and a top-of-the-order boost, he is our clear centerpiece. **Junior Caminero** (75.12) and **Christian Yelich** (74.05) follow closely, with the latter benefiting from a 13% boost due to dynamic platoon splits against Stock. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.08) remains a critical start despite facing a left-handed starter; his elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides the stolen base upside we prioritize, and his leadoff spot gives him the necessary volume to outweigh the platoon penalty.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the benching of **Pedro Ramirez**, who finished with a 53.99 score. While **Pedro Ramirez** offers switch-hitting versatility and positive SP skill adjustments, he was ultimately edged out by the superior efficiency and lineup placement of **Caleb Durbin** and **Hector Rodriguez**. The primary risk today centers on the middle infield; **Trea Turner** (53.24) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.75) are both facing a tough matchup against Woo, whose 3.59 xERA limits their output. Furthermore, **Dillon Dingler** (46.35) remains a marginal play as he faces Peralta, though his 5th-order slot keeps him just above our bench threshold. We will monitor the weather for any late-breaking wind shifts that could further dampen the production of **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** in what looks to be a challenging clash with elite pitching.",
